{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short", "label": "The Questions Still Open, Short Version (R1 to R19)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One-page sheet for the AMPM review of 26 October 2026, status open: one line per question, nineteen questions remaining after AMPM's answers of 25 October. Nine need a decision, ten need only a tick if AMPM agrees with the proposal; AMPM may tick a box, write on the line, or reply by number. Printed length three pages. The full version (Part A7) explains each question with what AMPM's documents say and the choices. When the sheet comes back the answers are recorded next to the 25 October answers and the drafts move to version 0.3."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_conflict", "label": "CONFLICT callout: two points to look at first", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Flagged at the top of the sheet because the two sources disagree and the rest of the answers depend on it: AMPM's compiled answers say the two family representatives share one login while AMPM's brief says separate accounts are preferable (see R5); the brief says the demo shows 'up to two' hotels per location while its closing note mentions one (see R1)."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_decide_nine_questions", "label": "Group: Decide - nine questions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The nine questions that need a decision from AMPM rather than a tick: R1, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7, R8, R11, R17. Grouped first so AMPM sees the decisions it cannot delegate to a proposal before the proposals it can simply accept."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_tick_if_you_agree_ten_proposals", "label": "Group: Tick if you agree - ten proposals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ten points where a proposal is already on the table and a tick is enough if AMPM agrees: R2, R9, R10, R12, R13, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19. Separated from the nine decisions to keep the sheet to one reading pass."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_small_defaults", "label": "Small defaults", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight unnumbered defaults collected at the foot of the sheet, each a tick or a blank: accounting export for AMPM's accountant (CSV, Tally, Zoho Books, other); website analytics and a bot check on the forms; who at AMPM signs each phase's acceptance; emergency reading of identity documents by the Super Admin, audited (allowed, two people, never); RSVP reminders then a call from the RSVP team with no guest edits after the deadline; readiness checklists hidden from the client; programme and calendar files to guests once invitations go out; one subscription per client account covering that client's weddings. Kept off the numbered list because none of them changes the shape of the build."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r1", "label": "R1: The demo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L11", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "How long the demo lasts, how many hotels per location, real or invented hotels. Proposal: 7 days, three locations, two hotels each, real hotels with indicative prices. Options: agree / duration ___ / hotels per location ___ / invented hotels instead. One of the two CONFLICT points: the brief says 'up to two' hotels per location while its closing note mentions one."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r2", "label": "R2: Payment gateway", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L32", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: Razorpay, unless AMPM already has a merchant account elsewhere. Options: agree / use ___."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r3", "label": "R3: Refunds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rule if a client wants the Rs 50,000 back. Proposal: no refund once the subscription is activated; full refund if AMPM cancels before activation. Options: agree / cooling-off period of ___ / case by case."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r4", "label": "R4: Web as well as apps", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whether clients also use hotel discovery and the wedding portal in a browser on a laptop. Proposal: yes, built from the same code as the client app; the team app stays native only. Flagged as the largest open cost item. Options: apps only / apps plus web (proposal) / web for clients, apps for the team."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r5", "label": "R5: Representative logins", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One shared login for the two family representatives or one account each. Proposal: one account per representative with the same rights on the same wedding, so every approval carries a name. Options: two accounts (proposal) / one shared login. One of the two CONFLICT points: the compiled answers say one shared login, the brief prefers separate accounts."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r6", "label": "R6: Approvals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whether one representative's approval completes a decision or both must approve. Proposal: one, with a setting to require both for budgets and contracts later. Options: one approval (proposal) / both for budgets and contracts / both for everything."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r7", "label": "R7: Money the client sees", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: planned and approved amounts per function, invoices issued to the client and their payment status; actual spend stays internal; never vendor quotes, costs or margins. Options: agree / approved amounts only / also actual spend and variance."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r8", "label": "R8: Hotel services with a fee", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Availability checks are included in the subscription. Proposal: negotiation, site visits, contract review and booking assistance need a recorded service agreement first. Options: agree / all included in the subscription / fee only on ___."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r9", "label": "R9: Staff roles and costs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: the nine roles from AMPM's specification; hotel costs visible to Super Admin, Finance, the Hotel Team and the Project Manager for their own weddings; vendor costs to Super Admin, Finance, the Vendor Coordinator and the Project Manager for their own weddings; nobody else. Options: agree / changes ___."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r10", "label": "R10: Staff sign-in", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: password plus a code from an authenticator app, which works without signal inside a venue. Options: agree / SMS OTP / Google Workspace or Microsoft 365."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r11", "label": "R11: RSVP links", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: a link per side as the standard, a combined link as an option per wedding, both in the first release; private links per household where AMPM has every household's contact. Options: agree / per side only / combined only / per household only."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r12", "label": "R12: Retention and privacy wording", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: leads 24 months after closing; guest records 12 months after the wedding closes; identity documents 30 days after checkout; nothing is deleted until a Super Admin approves the list; privacy wording drafted for AMPM's approval. Options: agree / periods ___ / wording approved by ___."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r13", "label": "R13: Hosting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L40", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: Amazon Web Services in Mumbai with copies in Hyderabad, all data in India; at most 15 minutes of data lost and the platform back within 4 hours; accounts and source code in AMPM's name. Options: agree / provider ___ / tighter recovery targets."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r14", "label": "R14: Capacity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "200 hotels and 20 weddings at a time, as AMPM said; the two missing figures are requested. Blanks: staff now ___ / in two years ___ / largest wedding ___ guests."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r15", "label": "R15: Messaging providers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L44", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: the developer selects the WhatsApp and SMS providers; AMPM owns the accounts and starts the WhatsApp and SMS registrations in the first week, since they take two to six weeks. Options: agree / use ___ / WhatsApp account owner at AMPM ___."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r16", "label": "R16: Service levels and support", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L46", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: 99.5 percent monthly availability, on-call cover from the developer on wedding days, no deployments while a wedding is live. Options: agree / office hours only / higher target."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r17", "label": "R17: Launch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything on one go-live or hotel discovery first. Proposal: hotel discovery goes live at the end of the first build phase and the wedding modules follow together; the schedule and the cost estimate wait for this answer. Options: discovery first (proposal) / one go-live / phase by phase."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r18", "label": "R18: Material changes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: a change is material at 10 percent on a budget line or 5 percent of the total budget, and on any date or venue change; the Project Manager approves it, and senior management too above 15 percent of the total. Options: agree / thresholds ___ / approval rule ___."}, {"id": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r19", "label": "R19: Archiving", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposal: a reminder before the three months end; the Project Manager proposes archiving and the Super Admin approves; afterwards the client sees only a contact route; reopening on request is read-only for 30 days. Options: agree / changes ___."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short", "target": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_decide_nine_questions", "target": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r1", "target": "docs_review_remaining_questions_r1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short", "target": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L32", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_tick_if_you_agree_ten_proposals", "target": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L32", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r2", "target": "docs_review_remaining_questions_r2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L32", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short", "target": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_r3", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/remaining-questions-short.md", "source_location": "L13", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_remaining_questions_short_decide_nine_questions", "target": "docs_review_re